# Markdown: numbered lists with Number markers per level, and lists written with 1) that number with a parenthesis.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Markdown · Numbered lists
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Markdown
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Numbered lists
		Paragraph: Lists written with `1.` are numbered with `Number markers`, one per level: `decimal`, `lower-alpha`, `upper-alpha`, `lower-roman` or `upper-roman`. A list written with `1)` takes a parenthesis instead of a period. A list that starts at another number keeps it.
			Style: intro
		Text: Number markers: decimal lower-alpha lower-roman
			Style: label
		Markdown:
			Number markers: decimal lower-alpha lower-roman
			Content >>
				1. Switch off the power.
				2. Remove the cover.
				   1. Keep the screws.
				   2. Lift the front.
				      1. From the bottom edge.
				      2. Without forcing it.
				3. Connect the wires.
		Text: Number markers: upper-roman, written with 1)
			Style: label
		Markdown:
			Number markers: upper-roman
			Content >>
				1) Scope of the agreement.
				2) Duration.
				3) Termination.
		Text: Number markers: upper-alpha, starting at 4
			Style: label
		Markdown:
			Number markers: upper-alpha
			Content >>
				4. Fourth appendix.
				5. Fifth appendix.
